c.com"},{"content_hash":"613824ee9b39c6c0a01462ed8ccfe7fbf6027e0e740c8d07abd20cf5a10ddb06","event_uuid":"bf1607d8-610f-40f6-a7fd-95752ed06405","position":{"commit_sha":"51dca9c9ba6e523cdecf83eef57aba0c9784877a","position":"1786208574624684001-bf1607d8-610f-40f6-a7fd-95752ed06405"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7a87ca417456ccfbc06ffc81fa3fee19df4fbcc773a2a822c88232b7a7dd5588","event_uuid":"a3cf8c53-e29c-48a1-92bf-5c786214f1ca","position":{"commit_sha":"da0d2d14e55778d1f2d139b62308a58552dcf41e","position":"1786209522063246001-a3cf8c53-e29c-48a1-92bf-5c786214f1ca"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation landed for review as Gerrit change 1548 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1548). Renumbered 22 duplicate-numbered ADRs to 0070-0091 (ascending landing-date order, earliest keeps its number); added 91 per-number marker files, generated docs/adr/README.md index + RENUMBERING.md, scripts/check_adr_numbers.py (CI bijection + referential-integrity gate) and scripts/gen_adr_index.py (--check drift mode), both wired into _build-and-test.yml. Rewrote slug-bearing cross-references across docs/ and src/. Local validation: 19/19 scripts tests GREEN (happy + held-out edge), mutation check confirms the gate flags dup-number/missing-marker/dangling-ref, real-tree check exit 0, make lint + make typecheck clean, ADR-index + env-vars drift guards exit 0. Awaiting Verified +1 and LLM-Review +1.","timestamp":1786209522063246001}],"created_at":1786046944815090001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d64f3295-0330-427a-aa7d-0e2c6ccafea0","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf"},{"link_uuid":"4a5a89d0-06f7-4eff-a1a1-acf8ea1920de","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1de3-a19f-c4ea-4b28"},{"link_uuid":"558d0e12-5eb3-4852-bd4d-eba46e52fc20","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"8537-78ba-fe3f-42d9"},{"link_uuid":"cf0841f6-47c8-4158-ae64-9d303d4225a6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4fbd-b4e0-3fe5-47c8"}],"description":"`docs/adr/` holds 83 files but only 61 distinct numbers. 17 numbers are reused — including FIVE\nunrelated ADRs numbered 0037, all `Status: Accepted`, all flat in one directory. There is no index.\nMeanwhile `AGENTS.md:42` cites \"ADR 0025\" by bare number and `CONTRIBUTING.md:173` sanctions bare\nADR references in commit trailers.\n\nDesign work established the cause and the safe remediation:\n\n**Cause.** Every collision landed within ~3 hours median. But only 6 of 22 were true in-flight\nGerrit races; 16 of 22 were stale-base — the earlier ADR had already landed and the author never\nrefetched. A pre-merge check would have caught 16 of 22.\n\n**Prevention is git's, not CI's.** A pre-merge uniqueness check on a monotonic counter is racy by\nconstruction, and ADR 0047 explicitly accepts that a change may land without re-running CI after a\nserver-side rebase. The race-free mechanism is a per-number marker file `docs/adr/.numbers/NNNN`\nwhose content is the ADR's filename: two ADRs claiming one number produce an add/add conflict,\nwhich Rebase-If-Necessary cannot auto-resolve. Empirically tested in throwaway repos: conflict iff\nsame number, ZERO false conflicts. A shared sorted index was tested and rejected — it conflicts on\nEVERY concurrent addition (~23% of this repo's ADR additions would conflict spuriously), and a\ncontributor would resolve it by regenerating, silently producing an index containing both.\n\n**Renumbering is approved** (limited user base). Earliest-landed keeps the number; 22 files move to\nnumbers above 0061. Historical disambiguation: ancestry alone resolves 23 of 90 commit references,\nco-landing 40, topic-matching 86 — 4 remain ambiguous and only 1 resists human resolution.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/adr/.numbers/NNNN` marker files exist for every ADR, content = the ADR filename\n- [ ] CI asserts the bijection between ADRs and markers, and that no two markers share content\n- [ ] A generated `docs/adr/README.md` index exists, grouped by workstream, showing full slugs\n- [ ] `docs/adr/RENUMBERING.md` records the old-to-new mapping and the per-reference resolution table, with tiers marked and the unresolvable reference recorded as UNRESOLVED\n- [ ] The 17 duplicate numbers are resolved, earliest-landed keeping the number\n- [ ] Moved ADRs carry a \"previously numbered\" header; kept ADRs carry an ambiguity-window note\n- [ ] `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md:602`'s ADR range citation is replaced by an explicit list\n## CURRENT-STATE CORRECTION (the header figures are stale; superseded here)\n\nThe description's \"83 files / 61 distinct numbers / above 0061\" reflects the board at ticket-creation\ntime. As of this implementation the ADR corpus grew (the sibling comment-triage shards 9ce8/4b94/ad16/ab77\nlanded NEW ADRs 0062-0069). Authoritative current state, re-measured from the tree:\n\n- **91 ADR files**, 69 distinct numbers, **17 duplicate numbers** (5x0037; 3x0007, 3x0035; and 0008-0012,\n  0015, 0016, 0026, 0031, 0032, 0036, 0038, 0040, 0041 doubled) = **22 files to move**.\n- **Moved ADRs are renumbered to 0070-0091** (NOT \"above 0061\" — 0062-0069 are now taken by the landed\n  sibling ADRs). Target range chosen to sit strictly above the highest existing number (0069).\n- Tiebreak unchanged: **earliest-landed keeps its number**; the 22 movers are assigned 0070..0091 in\n  ascending landing-date order (full git history, not the shallow-clone graft point). The exact old->new\n  map is recorded in docs/adr/RENUMBERING.md and is the authoritative artifact for AC \"resolve the 17\n  duplicate numbers\".\n\nAll seven acceptance criteria stand as written; only the numeric targets (file count, and the 0070-0091\ndestination band) are corrected here.\n\n## Cross-reference handling — stale-reference remediation (addresses plan-review T7/E6)\n\nRenumbering strands references. A reference to a MOVED ADR's old number now resolves to the KEPT ADR\nof that collision group (wrong target); a reference that always meant the kept ADR stays correct.\nThis is handled explicitly, not left to chance:\n\n**Sweep + resolve.** Every `ADR NNNN` / `adr/NNNN-slug` reference in `docs/` and `src/` (outside\n`docs/adr/` file bodies) that names a collision number is resolved to the SPECIFIC ADR it means (by\nadjacent slug when present, else by topic/context), and rewritten to that ADR's FINAL number. The\nper-reference resolution and its tier (slug-exact / topic-matched / ancestry / UNRESOLVED) is the\nresolution table already required by AC \"RENUMBERING.md\".\n\n**Worked example.** `docs/architecture.md` mentions \"the transport retry policy (ADR 0037)\". The\n0037 group keeps `0037-oss-contribution-intake-posture` (earliest-landed) and moves\n`0037-transport-retry` -> **0087**. The slug \"transport retry\" disambiguates: this reference meant\nthe moved ADR, so it is rewritten to `ADR 0087`. A bare \"ADR 0037\" whose context is OSS-intake stays\n`0037` (it now correctly names the sole surviving 0037).\n\n**Proving command (new AC below).** A referential-integrity assertion in the same CI check\n(`scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`) fails when any `adr/NNNN-slug` link in `docs/` points to a filename\nthat does not exist, or any `docs/adr/*.md` body cross-links a slug/number with no matching file.\nThis turns \"no stranded reference\" into an enforced, reproducible check rather than a claim. (Bare\nprose \"ADR NNNN\" with no slug is advisory-only — it cannot be mechanically bound to one ADR — and any\nresidue is recorded UNRESOLVED in RENUMBERING.md.)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (addendum — supersedes nothing, adds the T7/E6 proving path)\n\n- [ ] No stranded ADR cross-reference remains: every `adr/NNNN-slug` link in `docs/` (and every\n      slug/number cross-link inside `docs/adr/*.md`) resolves to an existing, unique ADR file, and\n      references that named a MOVED ADR are rewritten to its new 0070-0091 number. `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`\n      asserts this referential integrity (proving command: the check exits non-zero on a dangling\n      `adr/*-slug` link), and RENUMBERING.md records each rewritten reference with its resolution tier.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/","reason":"NEW per-number marker files (one per ADR, content = ADR filename); race-free uniqueness via add/add conflict on duplicate claim"},{"path":"scripts/check_adr_numbers.py","reason":"NEW CI check: ADR<->marker bijection, no two markers share content, no two ADRs share a number, AND referential integrity (no dangling adr/NNNN-slug link in docs/ or docs/adr cross-links)"},{"path":"tests/scripts/","reason":"NEW held-out TDD tests for check_adr_numbers.py (happy-path + held-out edge/E2E: dup number, missing marker, dup marker content, dangling reference)"},{".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml":"","path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"wire the ADR-number bijection + reference-integrity check into CI (guarded skip-if-absent pattern)"},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"NEW generated index grouped by workstream, full slugs"},{"path":"docs/adr/RENUMBERING.md","reason":"NEW old->new mapping + per-reference resolution table (tiers: slug-exact/topic/ancestry/UNRESOLVED)"},{"path":"docs/adr/","reason":"rename 22 duplicate-numbered ADRs to 0070-0091 (earliest-landed keeps number); 'previously numbered' header on moved, ambiguity-window note on kept"},{"path":"docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md","reason":"replace the ADR-range citation (~line 602) with an explicit list now that numbers moved"},{"path":"docs/","reason":"rewrite live adr/NNNN-slug references that named a MOVED ADR to its new 0070-0091 number"},{"path":"src/rebar/","reason":"rewrite any live ADR cross-references (in comments/docstrings) that named a MOVED ADR to its new number"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","managed_refs":[["depends_on","1de3-a19f-c4ea-4b28"],["depends_on","373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf"],["depends_on","8537-78ba-fe3f-42d9"],["parent","b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181"],["relates_to","4fbd-b4e0-3fe5-47c8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","parent_status_uuid":"aaf42a81-312b-46aa-bfd5-cd81898d255f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"0743-39a1-9689-409d","ticket_type":"story","title":"Make ADR numbers unique and collision-proof","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0efa9317-da0b-47cf-bde1-791997425196","d64f3295-0330-427a-aa7d-0e2c6ccafea0","4a5a89d0-06f7-4eff-a1a1-acf8ea1920de","558d0e12-5eb3-4852-bd4d-eba46e52fc20","30009cf1-60b5-4cc0-9951-fa9c9050adf8","1a006af7-8683-4b84-8c9b-a16416bc2b2f","0ea4e96a-1aa1-4273-a332-30a192156d76","2f4dc63e-421e-406d-b764-75af7c7f77f9","12510a10-a71a-47f8-8d19-8975800e650b","aaf42a81-312b-46aa-bfd5-cd81898d255f","bf1607d8-610f-40f6-a7fd-95752ed06405","a3cf8c53-e29c-48a1-92bf-5c786214f1ca","cf0841f6-47c8-4158-ae64-9d303d4225a6"]},"env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786209977802519323,"uuid":"b6d75ab0-cb2e-4cf6-8541-0d28ed9f6d47"}